%% Source: docs-src/guides/mal/authentication.md

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as User
    participant A as Your App
    participant MAL as MAL auth server
    participant API as MAL API

    U->>A: Start login
    A->>A: codeVerifier = random(43-128 chars)
    A->>A: codeChallenge = codeVerifier (plain PKCE)
    A->>A: buildMalAuthorizationUrl(clientId, codeChallenge, state)
    A->>U: Redirect to MAL authorize URL
    U->>MAL: Authorize app
    MAL->>U: Redirect to callback?code=...&state=...
    U->>A: Arrive at callback
    A->>A: Validate state matches
    A->>MAL: getMalAccessToken(clientId, code, codeVerifier)
    MAL->>MAL: Verify codeChallenge = codeVerifier
    MAL->>A: access_token + refresh_token
    A->>API: new AniLink({ mal: { accessToken, refreshToken, clientId } })
    API->>A: Authenticated data

    Note over A,MAL: Token expires (expires_in seconds)
    A->>A: getMalTokenExpiry(token) < now - 60s?
    A->>MAL: refreshMalAccessToken(clientId, refreshToken)
    MAL->>A: New access_token (+ optional refresh_token)
    A->>API: Continue with fresh token